# This CITATION.cff file was generated to enable proper citation of this
# repository, and to drive the author metadata on the Zenodo DOI record
# once the Zenodo-GitHub integration is enabled and a release is cut.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this protocol, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "A Protocol for Meta-Analysis with Dependent Effect Sizes"
abstract: >-
  A step-by-step protocol, written in R, for conducting a meta-analysis
  when effect size estimates are statistically dependent (multiple
  estimates per study). The protocol covers data cleaning, preliminary
  analysis, the choice of the within-study correlation (rho), and five
  meta-analytic estimators (FE, RE, HE, CE, and the preferred CHE model).
  It then applies three corrections for publication bias (PET-PEESE,
  step-function selection models, and robust Bayesian meta-analysis,
  RoBMA), uses the z-plot and estimated selection weights to choose the
  primary correction, and estimates the meta-regression and best-practice
  predictions for all three corrections, ending with a sensitivity
  summary. It is illustrated throughout with a meta-analysis of social
  capital and economic growth (Xue, Reed, and van Aert, 2025), but every
  step applies to any meta-analytic database with dependent effect sizes.
